{"title": "Trapped Beacon", "pageid": 50591, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Trapped_Beacon", "categories": ["Act One Locations", "Environmental objects", "Traps"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:TrappedBeacon.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/4/4a/TrappedBeacon.png/250px-TrappedBeacon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/4/4a/TrappedBeacon.png/375px-TrappedBeacon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/4/4a/TrappedBeacon.png 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/4/4a/TrappedBeacon.png/250px-TrappedBeacon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"253\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/4/4a/TrappedBeacon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption>A Trapped Beacon on the side of the gallery in Grymforge</figcaption></figure>\n<p>A <b>Trapped Beacon</b> is a unique type of <a href=\"/wiki/Trap\" title=\"Trap\">Trap</a> that might be encountered in the <a href=\"/wiki/Grymforge\" title=\"Grymforge\">Grymforge</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/Act_One\" title=\"Act One\">Act One</a> of the game.\n</p><p>A Trapped Beacon is a defensive mechanism of clearly Sharran design, resembling a giant vertical ring chiselled of stone, with a brazier inside. There are five beacons standing in the plain sight on each side of the narrow gallery in <a href=\"/wiki/Grymforge\" title=\"Grymforge\">Grymforge</a>, that can be reached only after successfully resolving the <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Get_Past_the_Rubble\" title=\"Get Past the Rubble\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/33px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/44px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Get Past the Rubble\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Get_Past_the_Rubble\" title=\"Get Past the Rubble\">Get Past the Rubble</a>: four in pairs across one another, the \"pair\" for the last one is destroyed.\n</p><p>The whole gallery is thickly trapped with <a href=\"/wiki/Marble_Plate\" title=\"Marble Plate\">Marble Plates</a>, both rectangular and round ones (these are planted between the Beacons), all working as a joint system. Triggering any of plates turns the whole gallery into a veritable obstacle course, as Trapped Beacons work in a certain accordant rhythm with Gargoyle Statues at the both ends of the gallery.\n</p><p>Upon triggering any of traps here a <a href=\"/wiki/Turn-based_mode\" title=\"Turn-based mode\">Turn-based mode</a> is started automatically. Once in two turns each Trapped Beacon projects a jet of flame that reaches the opposite side of the gallery, dealing <span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-fire\">2d6</span>⁠<span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Fire\" title=\"Fire\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/8/84/Fire_Damage_Icon.png/20px-Fire_Damage_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/8/84/Fire_Damage_Icon.png/30px-Fire_Damage_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/8/84/Fire_Damage_Icon.png/40px-Fire_Damage_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Fire\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/8/84/Fire_Damage_Icon.png/20px-Fire_Damage_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/8/84/Fire_Damage_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Fire\" title=\"Fire\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-fire\">Fire</span></a> damage to any targets in its way. The paired Trapped Beacons produce the flame jets simultaneously, which allows the party to cross their \"firing line\" the next turn, when they take pause. The Gargoyle Statues, however, activate <b>each turn</b>, and unlike Beacons, their flame jets protrude for 15 meters <b>and</b> might make the target fall <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Prone_(Condition)\" title=\"Prone (Condition)\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8e/Prone_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Prone_Condition_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/8/8e/Prone_Condition_Icon.webp/38px-Prone_Condition_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/8/8e/Prone_Condition_Icon.webp/50px-Prone_Condition_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Prone\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8e/Prone_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Prone_Condition_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/8/8e/Prone_Condition_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Prone_(Condition)\" title=\"Prone (Condition)\">Prone</a> along with taking the damage.\n</p><p>Each Trapped Beacon must be detected as a trap and disarmed individually, but botching the Disarm Trap roll on any of them sets off the whole system of traps on the gallery.\n</p><p>However, passing the gallery to its end and getting behind the iron gate is worth doing, as it allows to obtain two notable items:\n</p>\n<ul><li><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-rare\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Protecty_Sparkswall\" title=\"The Protecty Sparkswall\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/7/7e/The_Protecty_Sparkswall_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-The_Protecty_Sparkswall_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/7/7e/The_Protecty_Sparkswall_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-The_Protecty_Sparkswall_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/7/7e/The_Protecty_Sparkswall_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-The_Protecty_Sparkswall_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/7/7e/The_Protecty_Sparkswall_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-The_Protecty_Sparkswall_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/7/7e/The_Protecty_Sparkswall_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/The_Protecty_Sparkswall\" title=\"The Protecty Sparkswall\">The Protecty Sparkswall</a> (one of possible parts of the <a href=\"/wiki/Sparkstruck_set\" title=\"Sparkstruck set\">Sparkstruck set</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Idol_of_Shar\" title=\"Idol of Shar\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/7/7e/Idol_of_Shar_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Idol_of_Shar_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/7/7e/Idol_of_Shar_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Idol_of_Shar_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/7/7e/Idol_of_Shar_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-Idol_of_Shar_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/7/7e/Idol_of_Shar_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Idol_of_Shar_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/7/7e/Idol_of_Shar_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Idol_of_Shar\" title=\"Idol of Shar\">Idol of Shar</a>, which can serve as a gift to <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Shadowheart\" title=\"Shadowheart\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/7/7e/Portrait_Shadowheart.png/25px-Portrait_Shadowheart.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/7/7e/Portrait_Shadowheart.png/38px-Portrait_Shadowheart.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/7/7e/Portrait_Shadowheart.png/50px-Portrait_Shadowheart.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Shadowheart\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/7/7e/Portrait_Shadowheart.png/25px-Portrait_Shadowheart.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/7/7e/Portrait_Shadowheart.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Shadowheart\" title=\"Shadowheart\">Shadowheart</a> to improve her attitude towards the player character.</li></ul>\n<p>A Trapped Beacon can be disarmed with the help of <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Sleight_of_Hand\" title=\"Sleight of Hand\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/25px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/38px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/50px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Sleight of Hand\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/25px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Sleight_of_Hand\" title=\"Sleight of Hand\">Sleight of Hand</a> skill, but the character must have a <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit\" title=\"Trap Disarm Toolkit\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit\" title=\"Trap Disarm Toolkit\">Trap Disarm Toolkit</a> in their inventory. Difficulty Class requirement is a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;15 Sleight of Hand Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;15 <a href=\"/wiki/Sleight_of_Hand\" title=\"Sleight of Hand\">Sleight of Hand</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a> roll.\n</p><p>After successful disarming, the very ring of a Trapped Beacon is depicted as crumbling into a stone rubble down from the gallery.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714234532\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nP